# Passwordless sudo for the wheel group, on a development device only.
#
# THIS GRANTS UNRESTRICTED ROOT TO ANY MEMBER OF wheel WITH NO PASSWORD. That is
# why it is a separate, opt-in subpackage and not part of the device package:
# installing it is the decision, exactly as with -fingerprint.
#
# Why it exists: the porthole toolbox is unusable without it. `porthole doctor`
# checks for it and ph-capture.sh refuses to arm anything, because every one of
# its steps is `sudo -n` and with a password prompt they all fail silently and
# leave an empty log discovered hours later. On 2026-09-20 a
# `porthole flash full --replace-rootfs` wiped the hand-made drop-in and every
# device-side tool started failing with "sudo: interactive authentication is
# required" until it was recreated by hand -- which is the reason this is
# packaged rather than remembered.
#
# %wheel, not a username: pmOS puts the device's user in wheel at install time
# and the package cannot know what that user is called.
#
# Do NOT install this on a phone you carry.
%wheel ALL=(ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
